// case: route-multisegment-capture-not-final
// what: a `:name...` segment captures the rest of the path, so placing it
//      anywhere but the final segment builds a route that can never match
//      what it says: `/files/:p.../x` would have to capture "the rest" and
//      then keep matching. The matcher refuses non-final multis defensively,
//      and the checker rejects them here so the dead route is loud instead
//      of a silent 404.
// expect-error: must end the path
route GET "/files/:p.../x" {
    return ok "unreachable"
}
